(3083281, 431154, 67841, '<td valign="top">Image is a tad busy - my eye is a little confused by the lack of distinction between the elements - might just be my personal taste.  Our feathered friend is almost smack dab in the center, too, which makes it seem more like a snapshot than a real deliberate &amp; thoughtfully composed work.  I''m pretty much a newbie here, though, so take my comments with a grain of salt - just ''cause I''m being critical doesn''t mean I think MY stuff is doing any better! Good luck!</td>', 'Image is a tad busy - my eye is a little confused by the lack of distinction between the elements - might just be my personal taste.  Our feathered friend is almost smack dab in the center, too, which makes it seem more like a snapshot than a real deliberate & thoughtfully composed work.  I''m pretty much a newbie here, though, so take my comments with a grain of salt - just ''cause I''m being critical doesn''t mean I think MY stuff is doing any better! Good luck!', '2006-12-03 10:53:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(3083284, 432895, 67841, '<td valign="top">Thank you for actually tilting your composition - which seemed to be the thrust of this challenge that many people seemed to only distantly aim for.  But it seems TOO angled &amp; done so for the mere sake of tilting instead of as an aid to emphasize any particular portion of the photo.  Horizon gets soft too - which wouldn''t be bad except there''s nothing really strong in the foreground to draw the eye''s attention to.  I''m pretty much a newbie here, though, so take my comments with a grain of salt - just ''cause I''m being critical doesn''t mean I think MY stuff is doing any better! Good luck!</td>', 'Thank you for actually tilting your composition - which seemed to be the thrust of this challenge that many people seemed to only distantly aim for.  But it seems TOO angled & done so for the mere sake of tilting instead of as an aid to emphasize any particular portion of the photo.  Horizon gets soft too - which wouldn''t be bad except there''s nothing really strong in the foreground to draw the eye''s attention to.  I''m pretty much a newbie here, though, so take my comments with a grain of salt - just ''cause I''m being critical doesn''t mean I think MY stuff is doing any better! Good luck!', '2006-12-03 10:54:25.000000', NULL, 1),
