(3095091, 432626, 39243, '<td valign="top">My apologies if my initial comment, in retrospect it sounded too harsh  I just reread it and I could have been nicer. In reading your explanation I can see there are some implied diagonals. Keep up the good work, the photo by itself is very nice. I am not sure how to change this for a wedding invite maybe you could post it in a thread and see what other people can do with it.  Good luck  and again my sincere apologies. <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Caltrop:</b></div><hr/><i> its a cute photo and all but did you happen to read the challenge? In case you didn''t it was called "Diagonal" and the intention was to incorporate the diagonal axis of the frame into your picture. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'My apologies if my initial comment, in retrospect it sounded too harsh  I just reread it and I could have been nicer. In reading your explanation I can see there are some implied diagonals. Keep up the good work, the photo by itself is very nice. I am not sure how to change this for a wedding invite maybe you could post it in a thread and see what other people can do with it.  Good luck  and again my sincere apologies.  Originally posted by Caltrop: its a cute photo and all but did you happen to read the challenge? In case you didn''t it was called "Diagonal" and the intention was to incorporate the diagonal axis of the frame into your picture. ', '2006-12-07 01:01:55.000000', NULL, 0),
