(3132782, 432657, 24454, '<td valign="top">For me?  I always notice the eyes first in a photo like this.   And what I see is such incredible devotion and such a connection between the dog and his owner.   Photos like this touch me very much.<br/> <br/>I missed this during the voting because I didn''t have time to finish voting in the diagonal challenge -- but in my opinion, this photo is very underrated!<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work!   I hope next time you are rewarded more appropriately for your good work :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'For me?  I always notice the eyes first in a photo like this.   And what I see is such incredible devotion and such a connection between the dog and his owner.   Photos like this touch me very much. I missed this during the voting because I didn''t have time to finish voting in the diagonal challenge -- but in my opinion, this photo is very underrated! Keep up the good work!   I hope next time you are rewarded more appropriately for your good work :) ', '2006-12-19 21:47:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(3138112, 431595, 17420, '<td valign="top">For those of you who don''t know, the Kibbie Dome is the football stadium at the University of Idaho. <br/> <br/>I took this photo because I thought it might make a good diagonal shot. I cleaned up the trash around the area and didn''t see the bottle when I took the shot or when I looked through the shots on the viewer. When I got home I debated going back the next day to get a better bottleless shot, but thought it might not be all bad. Now I wonder how I would have done if the bottle wasn''t there and I tried black and white.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the comments, this was my first photo and I feel I need all the help I can get!</td>', 'For those of you who don''t know, the Kibbie Dome is the football stadium at the University of Idaho.  I took this photo because I thought it might make a good diagonal shot. I cleaned up the trash around the area and didn''t see the bottle when I took the shot or when I looked through the shots on the viewer. When I got home I debated going back the next day to get a better bottleless shot, but thought it might not be all bad. Now I wonder how I would have done if the bottle wasn''t there and I tried black and white. Thanks for the comments, this was my first photo and I feel I need all the help I can get!', '2006-12-21 04:46:01.000000', NULL, 0),
